From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 09:58:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] zink: acquire a window buffer before a copy reads it

zink_blit tried a copy region before it looked at a source that is a
window's buffer, and zink_kopper_acquire_readback used a buffer that had
not presented as its own readback without acquiring an image. A copy
from a new swapchain with no image acquired then referenced the
resource in the batch, and zink_kopper_acquire_submit read
swapchain->images[dt_idx] with dt_idx UINT32_MAX, far outside the
array:

  zink_kopper_acquire_submit+0x1c (ldrb w9, [x8, #2], x8 = images + 0xffffffff * 0x1a8)
  <- zink_resource_copy_region <- util_try_blit_via_copy_region <- zink_blit
  <- tc_batch_execute ... <- kopperSwapBuffersWithDamage

On an A19 Pro (KosmicKrisp), Counter-Strike's software renderer
(ddraw on wined3d's OpenGL renderer) faulted there at its first flip
after it changed the display mode, which resized its window and so its
swap chain. A source that is a window's buffer now goes through
blit_native, which takes its readback, and a readback that is the
buffer itself acquires an image first when none is (the contents of a
buffer that never presented are undefined either way).

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-12-display-modes.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_blit.c   | 3 ++-
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_kopper.c | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_blit.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_blit.c
index 758dbe1..258acd2 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_blit.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_blit.c
@@ -424,7 +424,8 @@ zink_blit(struct pipe_context *pctx,
          if (blit_resolve(ctx, info, &needs_present_readback))
             goto end;
       } else {
-         if (try_copy_region(pctx, info))
+         /* a window's buffer is read through its readback (blit_native) */
+         if (!src->obj->dt && try_copy_region(pctx, info))
             goto end;
          if (blit_native(ctx, info, &needs_present_readback))
             goto end;
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_kopper.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_kopper.c
index f652972..42cf8bd 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_kopper.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_kopper.c
@@ -1039,6 +1039,11 @@ zink_kopper_acquire_readback(struct zink_context *ctx, struct zink_resource *res
    /* if this hasn't been presented or if it has data, use this as the readback target */
    if (res->obj->last_dt_idx == UINT32_MAX ||
        (res->obj->dt_idx != UINT32_MAX && cdt->swapchain->images[res->obj->dt_idx].age)) {
+      /* a new swapchain with no image acquired: the batch's acquire
+       * semaphore is the image's, so acquire one before it is read
+       */
+      if (res->obj->dt_idx == UINT32_MAX)
+         zink_kopper_acquire(ctx, res, UINT64_MAX);
       *readback = res;
       return false;
    }
